<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#companions-of-the-prophet">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Companions of the Prophet</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sahaba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Companions of the Prophet, in Arabic sahaba, are the people who knew or saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a> and believed in him. They include the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a>, his family and the early converts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, and their reports form the basis of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadith">hadith</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni Islam</a> regards them collectively as trustworthy, while Shia <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> judges them individually.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/companions-of-the-prophet.jpg" alt="Companions of the Prophet" width="320" height="507" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mohammed_im_kreis_seiner_gef%C3%A4hrten.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
